<title>USA: U.S. wheat group calls for EEP export subsidies.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat group calls for EEP export subsidies.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The North Dakota Wheat Commission said Thursday the United States needs Export Enhancement Program subsidies to counter European Union subsidies.</p>
<p>The comission said in a statement released here that it had written to Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman saying the department was sending mixed messages to the grain markets.</p>
<p>The group said that, on the one hand, Glickman has stated he is prepared to begin using EEP, while on the other hand U.S. officials have said there are no plans to restart the program.</p>
<p>&quot;These conflicting statements confuse U.S. producers, but probably not the EU, Argentina or the wheat boards in Canada and Australia,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;To them, the message is crystal clear -- the U.S. is not willing or likely to challenge their misguided actions in the world market,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
